# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
#
# The pinned Open CASCADE, in one place.
#
# The commit is the authoritative identity; the digest covers the one download
# of a tarball GitHub generates on demand from it. Both used to live in the
# `env:` block of .github/workflows/runtime-layout.yml, which was their only
# machine-readable owner. §21A-2b2b0b2b1 needs the same three facts outside a
# workflow, because the native inventory names Open CASCADE as a component and
# a component's version and source digest cannot be a property of the file that
# happens to build it. A second copy would be a second answer, so the workflow
# now reads this file rather than declaring the pin itself.
#
# The version is what the pinned tree reports as OCC_VERSION_COMPLETE. It is
# recorded here because nothing that runs owned it before: docs/build-occt.md
# quoted it and no script could ask.
#
# Sourced by .github/workflows/runtime-layout.yml and by
# tools/generate-native-inventory.sh. Keep it assignments only: it is read by a
# shell.

OCCT_TAG=V8.0.1
OCCT_VERSION=8.0.1
OCCT_COMMIT=b8f597c677811d1f9f4d8a97f5ae2825c0353a42
OCCT_SHA256=dba62b81078dd43cec23feba89432be301582341001edad1b93342ad8bda35ea
OCCT_ARCHIVE_URL=https://github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT/archive/b8f597c677811d1f9f4d8a97f5ae2825c0353a42.tar.gz
